WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.522 --> 00:00:02.497
- If your name is
mentioned and people say,

00:00:02.497 --> 00:00:04.286
"Oh, hell. Oh, damn."

00:00:04.286 --> 00:00:06.338
(laughs)

00:00:06.338 --> 00:00:08.123
I think you're doing something wrong.

00:00:08.123 --> 00:00:12.739
Courage is the most
important of all the virtues

00:00:12.739 --> 00:00:14.334
because without courage,

00:00:14.334 --> 00:00:16.396
you can't practice any other virtue.

00:00:16.396 --> 00:00:19.017
There's an African saying which is,

00:00:19.017 --> 00:00:23.209
"Be careful when a naked
person offers you a shirt."

00:00:23.209 --> 00:00:26.792
I thought that I had
caused the man's death

00:00:28.510 --> 00:00:31.368
because I had spoken his name.

00:00:31.368 --> 00:00:34.159
- She was an American poet
and civil rights activist.

00:00:34.159 --> 00:00:36.827
She's best known for her for
series of seven autobiographies

00:00:36.827 --> 00:00:40.432
which focuses on her childhood
and early adult experiences.

00:00:40.432 --> 00:00:41.892
She was respected as a spokesperson

00:00:41.892 --> 00:00:43.129
for black people and women

00:00:43.129 --> 00:00:46.102
and her works were considered
as a defense of black culture.

00:00:46.102 --> 00:00:47.786
She's Maya Angelou and here's my take

00:00:47.786 --> 00:00:49.572
on her top 10 rules for success.

00:00:49.572 --> 00:00:50.983
Rule number one is my personal favorite

00:00:50.983 --> 00:00:52.698
and make sure to stick
around all the way to the end

00:00:52.698 --> 00:00:53.859
for some special bonus clips.

00:00:53.859 --> 00:00:56.099
Also, as she's talking, if
there's something she says

00:00:56.099 --> 00:00:57.566
that really resonates with you,

00:00:57.566 --> 00:00:59.063
please write it down in the comments

00:00:59.063 --> 00:01:00.224
and put quotes around it

00:01:00.224 --> 00:01:02.438
so that other people
can be inspired as well.

00:01:02.438 --> 00:01:05.881
(soaring sound)

00:01:05.881 --> 00:01:08.322
- I have a painting by Phoebe

00:01:08.322 --> 00:01:10.848
(classical music)

00:01:10.848 --> 00:01:13.866
of a group that she calls
Sister Sookie's Funeral

00:01:13.866 --> 00:01:15.983
and they all the women
there about, nine women,

00:01:15.983 --> 00:01:17.974
and they all look like women

00:01:17.974 --> 00:01:21.349
in my grandmother's prayer meeting group.

00:01:21.349 --> 00:01:25.301
So, whenever I'm obliged to do something,

00:01:25.301 --> 00:01:29.100
I take that painting and
I look at that painting.

00:01:29.100 --> 00:01:31.421
There's an empty chair and I think,

00:01:31.421 --> 00:01:32.962
now what would Grandma do?

00:01:32.962 --> 00:01:34.400
What would she say?

00:01:34.400 --> 00:01:37.374
I can almost hear her voice saying,

00:01:37.374 --> 00:01:41.107
"Now sister, you know what's right.

00:01:41.107 --> 00:01:42.274
Just do right.

00:01:43.888 --> 00:01:45.300
You don't really have to ask anybody.

00:01:45.300 --> 00:01:48.659
The truth is, right may not be expedient,

00:01:48.659 --> 00:01:50.906
it may not profitable,

00:01:50.906 --> 00:01:54.096
but it will satisfy your soul."

00:01:54.096 --> 00:01:57.263
(gentle guitar music)

00:01:58.258 --> 00:02:00.836
It brings you the kind of protection

00:02:00.836 --> 00:02:03.419
that bodyguards can't give you.

00:02:04.347 --> 00:02:06.217
Try to be all you can be

00:02:06.217 --> 00:02:09.640
to be the best human being you can be.

00:02:09.640 --> 00:02:13.189
Try to be that in your
church, in your temple.

00:02:13.189 --> 00:02:15.923
Try to be that in your classroom.

00:02:15.923 --> 00:02:19.388
Do it because it is right to do.

00:02:19.388 --> 00:02:22.629
You see, people will know you

00:02:22.629 --> 00:02:26.379
and they will add their
prayers to your life.

00:02:27.495 --> 00:02:29.444
They'll wish you well.

00:02:29.444 --> 00:02:33.092
I think, if your name is
mentioned and people say,

00:02:33.092 --> 00:02:37.048
"Oh, hell. Oh, damn." (laughs)

00:02:37.048 --> 00:02:39.433
I think you're doing something wrong.

00:02:39.433 --> 00:02:41.417
But if you're name is
mentioned and people say,

00:02:41.417 --> 00:02:42.608
"Oh, she's so sweet."

00:02:42.608 --> 00:02:43.675
"He's so nice."

00:02:43.675 --> 00:02:45.342
"Oh, God bless her."

00:02:46.918 --> 00:02:48.259
There you are.

00:02:48.259 --> 00:02:50.767
So try to live your life

00:02:50.767 --> 00:02:54.016
in a way that you will not regret years

00:02:54.016 --> 00:02:57.599
of useless virtue and
inertia and timidity.

00:02:59.105 --> 00:03:01.688
Take up the battle, take it up.

00:03:03.708 --> 00:03:07.827
It's yours. This is your
life. This your world.

00:03:07.827 --> 00:03:09.791
I'll be leaving it long before you

00:03:09.791 --> 00:03:12.783
under the ordinary set of circumstances.

00:03:12.783 --> 00:03:15.530
You make your own choices.

00:03:15.530 --> 00:03:18.787
You can decide life isn't worth living

00:03:18.787 --> 00:03:20.676
and that would be the
worst thing you can do.

00:03:20.676 --> 00:03:22.593
How do you know so far?

00:03:24.211 --> 00:03:25.313
Try it.

00:03:25.313 --> 00:03:26.146
See.

00:03:27.265 --> 00:03:31.432
So, pick it up. Pick the battle
and make it a better world.

00:03:33.869 --> 00:03:35.452
Just where you are.

00:03:37.267 --> 00:03:38.114
Yes.

00:03:38.114 --> 00:03:40.317
And it can be better
and it must be better,

00:03:40.317 --> 00:03:42.004
but it is up to us.

00:03:42.004 --> 00:03:43.499
I mentioned courage

00:03:43.499 --> 00:03:48.198
and I would like to say
something else about that.

00:03:48.198 --> 00:03:50.606
Finding courage in the leaders

00:03:50.606 --> 00:03:53.634
and in you who will become leaders.

00:03:53.634 --> 00:03:57.634
Courage is the most
important of all the virtues

00:03:58.607 --> 00:04:00.020
because without courage,

00:04:00.020 --> 00:04:04.184
you can't practice any
other virtue consistently.

00:04:04.184 --> 00:04:08.908
You see? You can't be
consistently kind or fair

00:04:08.908 --> 00:04:10.741
or humane or generous,

00:04:13.560 --> 00:04:16.793
not without courage because
if you don't have it,

00:04:16.793 --> 00:04:19.222
sooner or later, you'll stop and say,

00:04:19.222 --> 00:04:21.948
"Eh, the threat is too much.

00:04:21.948 --> 00:04:24.533
The difficulty is too high.

00:04:24.533 --> 00:04:27.345
The challenge is too great."

00:04:27.345 --> 00:04:31.639
You know, I believe that
self love is very important.

00:04:31.639 --> 00:04:33.231
If you read my work,

00:04:33.231 --> 00:04:37.167
you know I'm always talking
about loving oneself.

00:04:37.167 --> 00:04:41.293
I never trust anybody who
tells me he or she loves me

00:04:41.293 --> 00:04:44.710
if the person doesn't
love herself or himself.

00:04:44.710 --> 00:04:47.670
There's an African saying which is,

00:04:47.670 --> 00:04:52.255
"Be careful when a naked
person offers you a shirt."

00:04:52.255 --> 00:04:55.509
(audience laughs)

00:04:55.509 --> 00:04:59.640
I mean if he had something,
he'd cover himself first, right?

00:04:59.640 --> 00:05:02.792
So I like to look at self love.

00:05:02.792 --> 00:05:06.965
It is very important that
it comes from within,

00:05:06.965 --> 00:05:09.280
that you have a sense of yourself

00:05:09.280 --> 00:05:12.292
so that when you walk into an office,

00:05:12.292 --> 00:05:16.209
you don't go alone, bring
your people with you.

00:05:17.573 --> 00:05:21.332
Bring everybody has loved you with you.

00:05:21.332 --> 00:05:23.710
Say, "Grandma, come on. Let's go."

00:05:23.710 --> 00:05:25.665
Great-Grandpa, you've
been dead all this time.

00:05:25.665 --> 00:05:26.954
Come on. Let's go.

00:05:26.954 --> 00:05:29.255
I have to in here and have an interview.

00:05:29.255 --> 00:05:31.870
Come on Auntie. Come on my friends.

00:05:31.870 --> 00:05:33.362
Come. Let's go."

00:05:33.362 --> 00:05:34.430
And when you walk in,

00:05:34.430 --> 00:05:37.172
people don't know what it is about you,

00:05:37.172 --> 00:05:39.417
that can't take their eyes off you.

00:05:39.417 --> 00:05:42.206
You may not be cute in the given sense.

00:05:42.206 --> 00:05:45.372
You may not be high-fashion model size

00:05:45.372 --> 00:05:47.280
in that particular sense.

00:05:47.280 --> 00:05:49.080
You may not be any of those things,

00:05:49.080 --> 00:05:51.580
but they can't take their eyes off you.

00:05:51.580 --> 00:05:55.558
And they say of you,
in this incredible way,

00:05:55.558 --> 00:05:57.796
which I don't understand, they say,

00:05:57.796 --> 00:06:00.650
"I don't know, but she has charisma."

00:06:00.650 --> 00:06:03.912
No. What you have is all
those people around you.

00:06:03.912 --> 00:06:06.081
(audience laughs)

00:06:06.081 --> 00:06:09.720
So think of that any time
you have anything to do.

00:06:09.720 --> 00:06:13.415
Bring everybody with you
that you can remember

00:06:13.415 --> 00:06:16.327
who has loved you and then you have

00:06:16.327 --> 00:06:19.415
that sense of having been paid for

00:06:19.415 --> 00:06:21.688
and when you walk in people will say now,

00:06:21.688 --> 00:06:24.196
"I think you're overqualified."

00:06:24.196 --> 00:06:26.772
If you don't laugh, you will die.

00:06:26.772 --> 00:06:28.654
You know, you really must laugh.

00:06:28.654 --> 00:06:31.640
And if every human being in
the world would admit it,

00:06:31.640 --> 00:06:35.278
he or she is the funniest
person you've every met.

00:06:35.278 --> 00:06:36.448
(laughs)

00:06:36.448 --> 00:06:37.513
And the truth is, I mean,

00:06:37.513 --> 00:06:41.124
some people just rather be
a little stodgy and boring

00:06:41.124 --> 00:06:42.942
and you know, but the truth is,

00:06:42.942 --> 00:06:46.775
they themselves know
that they are very funny.

00:06:49.133 --> 00:06:52.417
The sense of humor isn't in self defense

00:06:52.417 --> 00:06:56.999
against those who pretend not
to have any sense of humor

00:06:56.999 --> 00:07:01.903
and against the cruelties
of life. One must laugh.

00:07:01.903 --> 00:07:06.070
There's an African-American
song, 19th century, which

00:07:08.687 --> 00:07:10.202
is so great.

00:07:10.202 --> 00:07:11.035
It says,

00:07:11.035 --> 00:07:14.162
♫ When it look like the sun

00:07:14.162 --> 00:07:17.575
♫ Wasn't going to shine anymore

00:07:17.575 --> 00:07:21.742
♫ God put a rainbow in the clouds

00:07:22.655 --> 00:07:27.326
Imagine. And I've had so
many rainbows in my clouds.

00:07:27.326 --> 00:07:29.159
I had a lot of clouds.

00:07:30.397 --> 00:07:32.695
But I have had so many rainbows.

00:07:32.695 --> 00:07:36.558
And one of the things I do
when I step up on a stage,

00:07:36.558 --> 00:07:39.105
when I stand up to translate,

00:07:39.105 --> 00:07:42.316
when I go to teach my classes,

00:07:42.316 --> 00:07:44.497
when I go to direct a movie,

00:07:44.497 --> 00:07:48.664
I bring everyone who has
ever been kind to me with me.

00:07:49.998 --> 00:07:53.500
Black, white, Asian,
Spanish-speaking, Native American,

00:07:53.500 --> 00:07:55.527
gay, straight, everybody.

00:07:55.527 --> 00:07:58.011
I say, "Come with me.
I'm going on the stage.

00:07:58.011 --> 00:08:00.097
Come with me, I need you now."

00:08:00.097 --> 00:08:00.930
Long dead.

00:08:02.303 --> 00:08:03.271
You see?

00:08:03.271 --> 00:08:06.271
So I don't ever feel I have no help.

00:08:08.060 --> 00:08:11.351
I've had rainbows in my clouds.

00:08:11.351 --> 00:08:14.268
And the thing to do it seems to me,

00:08:15.355 --> 00:08:16.970
is to be prepare yourself

00:08:16.970 --> 00:08:20.518
so that you can be a rainbow
in somebody else's cloud.

00:08:20.518 --> 00:08:23.016
Somebody who may not look like you,

00:08:23.016 --> 00:08:25.723
may not call God the
same name you call God,

00:08:25.723 --> 00:08:28.335
if they call God at all. (laughs)

00:08:28.335 --> 00:08:29.375
You see?

00:08:29.375 --> 00:08:33.174
I may not eat the same dishes
prepared the way you do,

00:08:33.174 --> 00:08:38.090
may not dance your dances
or speak your language,

00:08:38.090 --> 00:08:40.590
but be a blessing to somebody.

00:08:41.825 --> 00:08:45.242
When I was seven and a half, I was raped.

00:08:50.807 --> 00:08:54.724
I won't say severely
raped, all rape is severe.

00:09:00.515 --> 00:09:04.682
The rapist was a person very
well known to my family.

00:09:08.311 --> 00:09:09.894
I was hospitalized.

00:09:14.576 --> 00:09:17.076
The rapist was let out of jail

00:09:18.978 --> 00:09:21.395
and was found dead that night

00:09:22.866 --> 00:09:24.702
and the police suggested

00:09:24.702 --> 00:09:28.119
that the rapist had been kicked to death.

00:09:29.705 --> 00:09:31.622
I was seven and a half.

00:09:32.678 --> 00:09:36.261
I thought that I had
caused the man's death

00:09:37.857 --> 00:09:40.357
because I had spoken his name.

00:09:43.077 --> 00:09:46.966
That was my seven and
a half year old logic.

00:09:46.966 --> 00:09:49.966
So I stopped talking for five years.

00:09:53.289 --> 00:09:55.816
Now, to show you again

00:09:55.816 --> 00:09:58.816
how out of evil there can come good,

00:10:00.784 --> 00:10:02.990
in those five years,

00:10:02.990 --> 00:10:06.823
I read every book in the
black school library.

00:10:09.275 --> 00:10:11.590
I read all the books I could get

00:10:11.590 --> 00:10:14.696
from the white school library.

00:10:14.696 --> 00:10:18.203
I memorized James Weldon
Johnson, Paul Laurence Dunbar,

00:10:18.203 --> 00:10:21.137
Countee Cullen, and Langston Hughes.

00:10:21.137 --> 00:10:23.536
I'm memorized Shakespeare.

00:10:23.536 --> 00:10:24.536
Whole plays.

00:10:26.307 --> 00:10:27.224
50 sonnets.

00:10:29.915 --> 00:10:32.367
I memorized Edgar Allen Poe.

00:10:32.367 --> 00:10:33.617
All the poetry.

00:10:35.619 --> 00:10:38.786
Never having heard it, I memorized it.

00:10:40.054 --> 00:10:41.806
I had Longfellow.

00:10:41.806 --> 00:10:43.846
I had Guy de Maupassant.

00:10:43.846 --> 00:10:45.580
I had Balzac.

00:10:45.580 --> 00:10:47.976
(sigh)

00:10:47.976 --> 00:10:49.728
Rudyard Kipling.

00:10:49.728 --> 00:10:52.791
I mean it was Catholic kind of reading

00:10:52.791 --> 00:10:55.208
and Catholic kind of storing.

00:10:56.886 --> 00:10:58.886
When I decided to speak,

00:11:00.417 --> 00:11:02.368
I had a lot to say

00:11:02.368 --> 00:11:06.588
and many ways in which
to say what I had to say.

00:11:06.588 --> 00:11:09.612
I listened to the black minister,

00:11:09.612 --> 00:11:12.694
I listened to the melody of the preachers,

00:11:12.694 --> 00:11:15.057
and I could tell when
they would start up on

00:11:15.057 --> 00:11:18.177
that kind of thing when we know they mean

00:11:18.177 --> 00:11:21.043
to take our souls straight to heaven

00:11:21.043 --> 00:11:24.788
or whether they meant to
dash us straight to hell.

00:11:24.788 --> 00:11:26.468
I understood it.

00:11:26.468 --> 00:11:31.378
So out of this evil, which
was a dire kind of evil,

00:11:31.378 --> 00:11:35.709
because rape on the body of a young person

00:11:35.709 --> 00:11:38.959
more often than not introduces cynicism

00:11:40.945 --> 00:11:45.781
and there's nothing quite
so tragic as a young cynic

00:11:45.781 --> 00:11:49.566
because it means the person
has gone from knowing nothing

00:11:49.566 --> 00:11:51.316
to believing nothing.

00:11:52.337 --> 00:11:55.754
In my case, I was saved in that muteness.

00:11:57.083 --> 00:12:00.083
You see, in the sordida, I was saved

00:12:01.647 --> 00:12:05.147
and I was able to draw from human thought,

00:12:06.540 --> 00:12:10.707
human disappointments and
triumphs enough to triumph myself.

00:12:12.118 --> 00:12:15.019
We don't understand talent.

00:12:15.019 --> 00:12:17.561
We don't understand electricity.

00:12:17.561 --> 00:12:21.728
We probably use one billion
of one billionth percentage

00:12:26.417 --> 00:12:28.955
a degree so infinitesimal

00:12:28.955 --> 00:12:31.979
that we couldn't even
say how little it is.

00:12:31.979 --> 00:12:35.240
You can plug into two holes in the wall,

00:12:35.240 --> 00:12:37.635
you can light up a cathedral,

00:12:37.635 --> 00:12:40.611
you can light up a synagogue,

00:12:40.611 --> 00:12:42.865
you can light up a temple,
- [Interviewer] Right.

00:12:42.865 --> 00:12:44.173
- You can light up a surgery

00:12:44.173 --> 00:12:48.209
or you can electrocute a
person strapped in a chair.

00:12:48.209 --> 00:12:50.013
Electricity makes no demands.

00:12:50.013 --> 00:12:51.473
It says, "I'm here."

00:12:51.473 --> 00:12:52.306
- [Interviewer] That's right.

00:12:52.306 --> 00:12:54.840
- If you are stupid, you will ill use me.

00:12:54.840 --> 00:12:56.423
If you are intelligent,

00:12:56.423 --> 00:13:00.506
you will use me for the
furtherance of your kind.

00:13:02.045 --> 00:13:05.175
Well I think talent is like that.

00:13:05.175 --> 00:13:07.237
We don't know what it is,

00:13:07.237 --> 00:13:10.446
but a painter maybe he or she is born

00:13:10.446 --> 00:13:14.770
with eyesight to see
depth and, you understand,

00:13:14.770 --> 00:13:16.024
- [Interviewer] Sure, sure.

00:13:16.024 --> 00:13:17.524
- That's physical.

00:13:18.908 --> 00:13:23.199
Maybe she is born with a
throat that makes a sound

00:13:23.199 --> 00:13:24.199
like a bird,

00:13:25.858 --> 00:13:27.371
a coloratura,

00:13:27.371 --> 00:13:30.099
lyric soprano, baritone.

00:13:30.099 --> 00:13:34.051
But singing has very
little to do with voice,

00:13:34.051 --> 00:13:38.425
it is okay but if it
was really about voice,

00:13:38.425 --> 00:13:41.362
Ray Charles and Willie
Nelson wouldn't be mentioned.

00:13:41.362 --> 00:13:43.666
- (laughs) It's true.

00:13:43.666 --> 00:13:46.066
I just did a story on autism

00:13:46.066 --> 00:13:49.624
and it was the people who couldn't write,

00:13:49.624 --> 00:13:53.728
couldn't express themselves,
but sang in pitch.

00:13:53.728 --> 00:13:54.561
- In pitch.

00:13:54.561 --> 00:13:56.449
- [Interviewer] And beautifully.

00:13:56.449 --> 00:14:00.616
- And can compute 40 columns
of three numbers each.

00:14:03.127 --> 00:14:04.808
- [Interviewer] That's right. Right.

00:14:04.808 --> 00:14:06.657
- They got it. (snaps fingers)
- How do they do that?

00:14:06.657 --> 00:14:07.490
That's talent.

00:14:07.490 --> 00:14:08.607
- That's talent.
- [Interviewer] (laughs)

00:14:08.607 --> 00:14:09.440
- I don't know it.

00:14:09.440 --> 00:14:11.346
I mean, I thank God I have it,

00:14:11.346 --> 00:14:14.452
but I think every person
born is born with talent.

00:14:14.452 --> 00:14:18.619
There's a place in you that
you must keep in inviolate.

00:14:20.073 --> 00:14:22.740
You must keep it pristine, clean

00:14:24.794 --> 00:14:27.852
so that nobody has the right to curse you,

00:14:27.852 --> 00:14:29.490
treat you badly, nobody.

00:14:29.490 --> 00:14:33.531
No mother, father, no
wife, no husband, nobody

00:14:33.531 --> 00:14:36.895
because that may be the place
you go to when you meet God.

00:14:36.895 --> 00:14:38.744
You have to have a place
where they just say,

00:14:38.744 --> 00:14:40.327
"Stop it. Back up."

00:14:41.587 --> 00:14:43.909
- [Oprah] Not here you want.
- You must. Not. No.

00:14:43.909 --> 00:14:44.742
- [Oprah] No.

00:14:44.742 --> 00:14:45.743
- Absolutely.

00:14:45.743 --> 00:14:48.953
And that's one I told you 25 years ago.

00:14:48.953 --> 00:14:49.786
- [Oprah] Yes.

00:14:49.786 --> 00:14:51.220
- Say no when it's no.

00:14:51.220 --> 00:14:52.053
- [Oprah] Yeah.

00:14:52.053 --> 00:14:52.886
- Say so.

00:14:52.886 --> 00:14:57.053
Back it up because that place
has to remain clean and clear.

00:14:58.396 --> 00:14:59.996
- And that has to be a
place within yourself.

00:14:59.996 --> 00:15:00.939
- [Maya] Yes, ma'am.
- Yeah.

00:15:00.939 --> 00:15:02.542
- [Interviewer] When
you're writing poetry,

00:15:02.542 --> 00:15:06.125
are you writing to
express your experiences

00:15:07.025 --> 00:15:09.872
or do you write to inspire other people?

00:15:09.872 --> 00:15:13.122
- No, I write to try to say what I see,

00:15:14.056 --> 00:15:16.059
what I've seen.

00:15:16.059 --> 00:15:20.205
And of course, I hope
that it's inspirational.

00:15:20.205 --> 00:15:22.282
- [Interviewer] When you were
writing Phenomenal Woman,

00:15:22.282 --> 00:15:24.707
did you realize how many millions of women

00:15:24.707 --> 00:15:27.028
would be inspired by that?

00:15:27.028 --> 00:15:30.232
- No. I didn't realize any of that.

00:15:30.232 --> 00:15:32.609
I just do the best I can.

00:15:32.609 --> 00:15:35.200
You may write me down in history

00:15:35.200 --> 00:15:37.481
with your bitter, twisted lies.

00:15:37.481 --> 00:15:40.290
You may trod me in the very dirt,

00:15:40.290 --> 00:15:42.957
but still, like dust, I'll rise.

00:15:44.977 --> 00:15:47.391
Does my sassiness upset you?

00:15:47.391 --> 00:15:49.763
Why are you beset with gloom?

00:15:49.763 --> 00:15:51.571
Just cause I (snaps fingers) walk as if

00:15:51.571 --> 00:15:53.203
I have got oil (snaps fingers) wells

00:15:53.203 --> 00:15:56.925
pumping in my living room.
(audience laughs)

00:15:56.925 --> 00:15:59.549
Just like moons and like suns,

00:15:59.549 --> 00:16:02.250
with the certainty of tides,

00:16:02.250 --> 00:16:06.493
just like hopes springing
high, still I rise.

00:16:06.493 --> 00:16:09.001
Did you want to see me broken?

00:16:09.001 --> 00:16:11.527
Bowed head and lowered eyes?

00:16:11.527 --> 00:16:14.639
Shoulders falling down like teardrops,

00:16:14.639 --> 00:16:17.056
weakened by my soulful cries?

00:16:18.021 --> 00:16:21.145
Does my sassiness upset you? (laughs)

00:16:21.145 --> 00:16:23.553
(audience laughs)
Don't you take it so hard

00:16:23.553 --> 00:16:27.525
just cause I laugh as if I have gold mines

00:16:27.525 --> 00:16:30.182
diggin' in my own backyard.

00:16:30.182 --> 00:16:32.519
You can shoot me with your words,

00:16:32.519 --> 00:16:35.068
you may cut me with your lies,

00:16:35.068 --> 00:16:37.038
you can kill me with your hatefulness,

00:16:37.038 --> 00:16:39.538
but just like life, I'll rise.

00:16:40.825 --> 00:16:44.175
Does my sexiness offend you? Awww.

00:16:44.175 --> 00:16:46.800
(audience laughs)

00:16:46.800 --> 00:16:50.967
Does it come as a surprise
that I dance (snaps fingers)

00:16:53.627 --> 00:16:57.420
as if I have diamonds at
the meeting of my thighs?

00:16:57.420 --> 00:16:59.781
(audience laughs)

00:16:59.781 --> 00:17:03.746
Out of the huts of
history's shame, I rise.

00:17:03.746 --> 00:17:07.587
Up from a past rooted in pain, I rise.

00:17:07.587 --> 00:17:10.544
A black ocean, leaping and wide,

00:17:10.544 --> 00:17:14.803
welling and swelling
and bearing in the tide.

00:17:14.803 --> 00:17:18.886
Leaving behind nights of
terror and fear, I rise.

00:17:19.989 --> 00:17:23.572
Into a daybreak
miraculously clear, I rise.

00:17:25.083 --> 00:17:28.332
Bringing the gifts that my ancestors gave,

00:17:28.332 --> 00:17:31.749
I am the hope and the dream of the slave.

00:17:33.284 --> 00:17:34.117
And so,

00:17:35.125 --> 00:17:36.392
(claps hands)

00:17:36.392 --> 00:17:38.639
(soaring sound)
(audience laughs)

00:17:38.639 --> 00:17:40.041
There I go.

00:17:40.041 --> 00:17:43.041
(audience applause)

00:17:45.283 --> 00:17:47.438
(soaring sound)

00:17:47.438 --> 00:17:48.611
- Thank you guys so much for watching.

00:17:48.611 --> 00:17:51.626
I am this video because
Kayla Maroon asked me to.

00:17:51.626 --> 00:17:53.072
So if there's a famous entrepreneur

00:17:53.072 --> 00:17:54.235
that you want me to profile next,

00:17:54.235 --> 00:17:56.516
leave it in the comments below
and I'll see what I can do.

00:17:56.516 --> 00:17:58.254
I'd also love to know what
you thought of the video.

00:17:58.254 --> 00:17:59.764
What clips resonated the most with you?

00:17:59.764 --> 00:18:02.718
What did you learn that's
going to change your business

00:18:02.718 --> 00:18:03.551
or your life?

00:18:03.551 --> 00:18:06.521
Leave it in the comments and
I will join in the discussion.

00:18:06.521 --> 00:18:08.605
Finally, I want to give a quick
shout out to Philip Norton.

00:18:08.605 --> 00:18:10.587
Philip, thank you so much
for buying a copy of my book.

00:18:10.587 --> 00:18:11.967
It really means a lot to me.

00:18:11.967 --> 00:18:13.037
Those of you guys watching,

00:18:13.037 --> 00:18:15.356
if you want your chance at a
shout out in a future video,

00:18:15.356 --> 00:18:17.243
make sure to pick up a copy of the book

00:18:17.243 --> 00:18:19.620
and email in your receipt
so we can keep track.

00:18:19.620 --> 00:18:21.286
Thank you guys so much for watching.

00:18:21.286 --> 00:18:24.333
Continue to believe, or
whatever your one word is.

00:18:24.333 --> 00:18:25.596
And I'll see you soon.

00:18:25.596 --> 00:18:28.263
(soaring sound)

00:18:32.126 --> 00:18:34.959
- If we've been able to stay alive

00:18:35.973 --> 00:18:38.806
at all, alive and future thinking.

00:18:41.603 --> 00:18:45.579
Alive and having enough
courage to care for each other.

00:18:45.579 --> 00:18:47.496
enough courage to love,

00:18:48.525 --> 00:18:52.826
and know that we're probably 1% free,

00:18:52.826 --> 00:18:55.076
1% of 60 million free,

00:18:59.160 --> 00:19:00.798
of complaints.

00:19:00.798 --> 00:19:02.798
Imagine who would we be?

00:19:05.939 --> 00:19:10.106
Who would we be if we
were 1% of 600 million?

00:19:11.655 --> 00:19:13.250
6 billion?

00:19:13.250 --> 00:19:14.906
What would happen?

00:19:14.906 --> 00:19:17.243
I'll tell you one thing,

00:19:17.243 --> 00:19:20.632
I think war would be
laughed out of the room.

00:19:20.632 --> 00:19:21.895
I think the very word,

00:19:21.895 --> 00:19:24.061
if somebody said, "War."

00:19:24.061 --> 00:19:25.269
Another person would say,

00:19:25.269 --> 00:19:26.601
"You mean, am I supposed to kill somebody

00:19:26.601 --> 00:19:27.898
because he doesn't agree with me?

00:19:27.898 --> 00:19:30.236
(laughs) I don't think so."

00:19:30.236 --> 00:19:31.949
Just imagine.

00:19:31.949 --> 00:19:34.108
People would speak kinder.

00:19:34.108 --> 00:19:37.052
More kindly to each other.

00:19:37.052 --> 00:19:41.100
Courtesy would be invited
back into the living room

00:19:41.100 --> 00:19:41.946
and into the bedroom

00:19:41.946 --> 00:19:43.809
and into the children's room,

00:19:43.809 --> 00:19:45.226
into the kitchen.

00:19:46.274 --> 00:19:48.191
If 1% of our world

00:19:52.476 --> 00:19:54.059
was complaint free,

00:19:55.847 --> 00:19:58.829
we would care more about the children

00:19:58.829 --> 00:20:01.485
and realize that every child is our child.

00:20:01.485 --> 00:20:03.280
The black one and the white one.

00:20:03.280 --> 00:20:05.033
The pretty one and the plain one.

00:20:05.033 --> 00:20:06.860
The Asian and the Muslim.

00:20:06.860 --> 00:20:09.000
The Japanese and the Jewish.

00:20:09.000 --> 00:20:10.833
Everyone is our child.

00:20:12.437 --> 00:20:15.937
If we were just 1% free of complaint,

00:20:18.098 --> 00:20:21.836
imagine that we would
start blaming other people

00:20:21.836 --> 00:20:23.253
for our mistakes.

00:20:24.492 --> 00:20:26.178
(laughs)

00:20:26.178 --> 00:20:27.173
And hating them

00:20:27.173 --> 00:20:31.654
because they caused the
mistake in our minds.

00:20:31.654 --> 00:20:35.237
Just imagine if we
laughed more frequently.

00:20:36.174 --> 00:20:38.591
If we had unmitigated courage

00:20:42.075 --> 00:20:43.742
to touch each other.

00:20:45.514 --> 00:20:49.431
It would just the beginning
of paradise in now.

00:20:50.974 --> 00:20:51.807
Thank you.

